    "What is my relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a challenging subject for me, more of an obstacle than a tool. While I appreciate its logical structure and precision, it lacks the depth or practical relevance that subjects like philosophy or economics offer. My education level stopped at upper secondary, so I never delved deeply into advanced topics. It’s functional for daily tasks but doesn’t captivate my interest.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, occasionally. Not because of the complexity itself, but because I feel a sense of inadequacy when faced with problems that require more abstract or technical knowledge than what I’ve learned. It’s not crippling anxiety, but it’s enough to make me avoid diving deeper into mathematical topics unless absolutely necessary.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I haven’t used AI for math learning recently, and I’m not sure I would. While I recognize its potential, I prefer traditional methods or self-study when I need to brush up on something. My approach is more intuitive, relying on logic rather than structured algorithms or tools.",
